    "description": "We’re looking for an experienced SAP Team Lead / Interim SAP Manager to lead an established SAP team within an international manufacturing business in Germany.\nOur client operates across multiple countries, with several businesses sharing a central SAP S/4HANA system. With ongoing acquisitions and SAP rollouts, they need someone who can lead the team, improve ways of working and ensure SAP continues to support the wider business.\nThe current SAP Team Lead is approaching retirement, allowing for a structured handover.\nThis is a leadership role, not a pure project management position. You'll need broad SAP knowledge, particularly SD and Logistics, alongside strong people management and business-facing skills.\nWhat you’ll do\nLead and develop an established SAP team of around 10 people.\nMentor consultants, improve team performance and establish clear priorities.\nWork closely with business departments to translate requirements into SAP solutions.\nChallenge unnecessary change requests and focus on business priorities.\nSupport ongoing S/4HANA rollouts and integration of acquired businesses.\nImprove team processes and ways of working.\nContribute to longer-term SAP strategy, including cloud migration and data initiatives.\nWhat we’re looking for\nStrong German language skills – essential.\nProven experience as an SAP Team Lead, SAP Application Manager or Head of SAP.\nStrong SAP SD and Logistics knowledge – essential.\nBroad SAP knowledge, ideally including WM, Production and FI/CO.\nExperience managing and developing SAP teams.\nStrong SAP S/4HANA knowledge and understanding of end-to-end business processes.\nAbility to bridge the gap between business stakeholders and technical teams.\nProactive leadership style with strong stakeholder management skills.\nSAP Fiori, cloud migration or acquisition integration experience would be advantageous.\nThe practical details\nStart: Mid-December 2026 / Early January 2027.\nContract: Long-term interim assignment, with an initial handover period.\nCommitment: 5 days per week.\nLocation: North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany.\nOnsite: 5 days per week initially, potentially reducing to 3 days after 4 months.\nInterview process: 2 stages.\nYou'll report to the Head of IT and play a key role in developing the SAP team while supporting ongoing transformation initiatives.\nPlease share your CV and availability for a call.\nKR,\nWill Reynolds\nEnergize SAP\n***@***.com\n***** / *****\n\nSkills: Interim Management, Projektmanagement, SAP ERP, SAP Financials, SAP Functional Consulting, SAP HANA, SAP Implementierung, SAP LE, SAP Logistik, SAP Projektmanagement, SAP SD, SAP-Integrationen, SAP Fiori",
